# Runtime dependencies. Every package is pinned to an exact version so a
# rebuild is reproducible and CVE exposure can't drift silently between builds
# (research DEP1). The versions below match what is running in production
# (captured from `pip freeze` in the deployed image), so pinning is a no-op for
# behaviour — it just freezes the known-good set. All have manylinux wheels for
# both linux/arm64 and linux/amd64 at these versions, so the multi-arch release
# build is unaffected.
#
# This file is the human-edited SOURCE of runtime deps (direct, pinned). It is
# compiled into requirements.txt, the fully-hashed transitive lock that the
# Docker image and PR CI install with `--require-hashes` (integrity — DEP1/DEP4).
# requirements-dev.in and requirements-ci.in work the same way.
#
# EDITING THIS FILE ALONE HAS NO EFFECT — the image installs from the lock, so a
# bump here that isn't compiled into the lock never reaches production.
# `backend/tests/test_requirements_lock_sync.py` fails the build if they drift.
#
# The `name.in` → `name.txt` layout with uv's header is the one Dependabot's uv
# ecosystem can regenerate: it edits the pin here and reruns the command from
# the lock's header. By hand, recompile both locks with those commands; they are
# universal, so any machine resolves them for arm64 and amd64 alike, and uv
# keeps every pin it is not forced to move:
#
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --universal --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file=requirements.txt requirements.in
#   uv pip compile --generate-hashes --universal --python-version 3.12 \
#       --output-file=requirements-dev.txt requirements-dev.in
#
# Then prove it installs before committing. The release image is arm64 and PR CI
# builds only amd64, so check that a bumped native package has an arm64 wheel.
# Ask for manylinux_2_28: pikepdf, onnxruntime and pillow-heif ship no
# manylinux2014 wheels any more, so that platform finds nothing.
#
#   pip install --dry-run --require-hashes -r requirements.txt
#   pip download --only-binary=:all: --platform manylinux_2_28_aarch64 \
#       --python-version 3.12 --no-deps <package>==<version> -d <scratch-dir>
fastapi==0.141.1
